WEBVTT

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.980
SWORD GAI

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.990
<i>Approaching destination point, Marcus!</i>

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.120
Roger.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:26.870
Good luck!

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.980
E-Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.360
Azoth Sword!

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.570
Call the darkness, Beelzebub!

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.410
What?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.250
My body won't...

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.420
I'm not your enemy.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.550
I'm not interested in
what you rebels are up to.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.300
Then what do you want?

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.680
Give me the Pyramid Dau.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.100
That weapon isn't something
you can control.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.180
Tell me. Where is the Pyramid Dau?

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.900
Th-The captain... has it!

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.900
Sleep for a while.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:54.590
I was too late!

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.380
Beelzebub!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.690
I've recovered the Pyramid Dau.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.440
You did well. Good work.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.030
Were you injured?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.950
<i>I'm fine. Thanks.</i>

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.540
<i>As soon as you've turned in
<i>the Pyramid Dau, please get examined.</i></i>

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:32.580
<i>If nothing's wrong, you can take a 24-hour
<i>break before reentering cold sleep.</i></i>

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.420
Please wait a second.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.550
<i>There's been something bothering me
<i>that I haven't told you.</i></i>

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.840
Is there a problem?

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.140
The numbers all looked fine.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:48.430
For this mission,
I was active for 72 hours.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.350
Before that, I was in cold sleep
for three days, or another 72 hours.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.320
For Chrysalises like us,
isn't cold sleep a form of labor?

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:03.860
<i>That means I've been working a total
<i>of 144 hours in a row.</i></i>

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:08.240
<i>I think there's a serious problem
<i>with the Shoshidai's working conditions.</i></i>

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.700
What are you saying?

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.250
I'm sorry.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.830
I was joking.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.880
But I do have a request.
Can you extend my break?

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.550
<i>To a week? Or at least three days?</i>

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.760
Fine. I'll consider it.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.140
He's changed, huh?

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:31.270
Yes.
I never expected him to joke like that.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.640
Maybe he's settling into the job.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:36.100
Aya?

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.690
Yeah, I'm fine. The mission's over.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.360
Kyoka agreed to give me an extended break.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.400
Yeah, got it.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.070
I can't wait to see you.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:49.740
Me either.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.410
I've been thinking about you
the whole time.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.000
I know. Bye.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.520
Seriously, stop crying already, Rie!

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.770
Shoko.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.690
But... but it's going to hurt today!

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.740
Crying won't make the exams
or the treatment stop.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.070
But I don't like that it hurts!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.870
Yeah. Me neither.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.000
You're always gloomy on exam days too,
Shoko.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.130
When will we get to leave this place?

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.590
Will we be here forev--

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.800
Of course not! Stop saying weird things.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.100
That's right!
What will you do when you're discharged?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.520
This again?
I've told you a bunch of times.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:00.480
First, I'll go eat all the barbecue I can.
The food here is awful.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.730
Maybe I'll go with you.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:06.820
Really? Weren't you going to swim
at a tropical island?

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.570
We can just eat barbecue
on a tropical island!

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.160
Great idea!

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:16.620
You come too, Rie! Once we're out,
let's eat barbecue on a tropical island!

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.620
No. I want to be with Brother.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.920
Don't worry.
You can see him on visiting day.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.420
Rie's really obsessed with her brother.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.300
Doctor.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.930
It's almost time, Rie.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.680
No! I don't want to hurt!

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:38.390
Yes, but it's so you can get better.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.350
So you have to endure it.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.270
Okay.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.860
I know! On the next field trip,
I'll take you to a place you like.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.490
Really?

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:51.530
Yeah. I promise.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.700
So you can do this, right?

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.040
Yeah.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.290
This feels so good!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.670
This is wonderful, Marcus.
I wouldn't care if I died!

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.550
Hold on! I'd be sad if you died.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.510
You've been doing great lately though,
Marcus.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.890
Administrator Kagami complimented you.
She said you're all grown up.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.640
You're looking a little more manly too,
right?

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.100
Is that a compliment?

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:05.900
Yes, it is.

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:11.030
I decided that worrying wasn't helping me.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.700
My only option now is to live
at the Shoshidai.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.910
So I'll work as hard as I can
for the Shoshidai.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.620
That's great, Marcus.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.290
Impressed?

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.540
Yeah.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.630
And I'm also surprised
you know how to pilot a yacht.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.840
I was in the yacht club in college.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.970
I once won a tournament.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.260
Dad bought me this yacht back then
to celebrate.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:37.930
Wow!

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:42.680
If you'd lived a normal life, you
never would've talked to a girl like me.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:46.730
What are you talking about?
I'm content with my life right now.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:52.070
Because I... met you.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.830
I... I want to get married!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:01.790
I'm sure you will!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.500
They're working on a medicine
called Prismaphon at the Shoshidai.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.340
Once it's done, Chrysalises
and Busoma can go back to normal--

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.710
That's not what I mean!

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.840
I want to marry you right now!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.720
I need you!

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.050
So...

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.100
is that okay?

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.100
It's okay.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.480
Really?

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:24.560
Really really?

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:33.740
Let's have a long kiss.
One worthy of Guinness.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:35.990
<i>Guinness?</i>

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.490
Is something wrong?

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.120
No, nothing.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:45.080
I'll become a man you can really count on!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.420
I don't want to disappoint you!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.500
I'll be cheering you on.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.130
I don't get it.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.170
What are you worried about?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:57.800
I've heard Marcus Lithos's tests
are all coming back normal.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.390
Yes, that's right.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:05.600
The Maldicion values in his blood
are very low for a Chrysalis.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:11.060
Based on the tests, there's no reason
to think he'll become a Busoma soon.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.270
Then what is it?

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.110
The numbers are too good.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.990
Marcus has been on four missions
in the past three months.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.780
Despite all those missions,
his Maldicion values haven't changed.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:26.870
The amount of time a Chrysalis takes
to become a Busoma varies,

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.580
and we don't yet know
the mechanism behind it.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.500
Doesn't this imply
that Marcus's moratorium is longer?

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:35.000
Yes.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:39.760
I would've assumed so as well,
if his Core Alma wasn't the Azoth Sword.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.760
What does that mean?

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:45.770
The Azoth Sword isn't a normal Sage Alma.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.900
The weapons we keep here became Sages
after absorbing a lot of blood.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.480
But the Azoth Sword
contains the demon Beelzebub,

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:58.190
sealed within it by the wizard Paracelsus.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.160
We're up against a demon.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.250
Who should we invite to the ceremony?
Definitely Miki.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.300
<i>That's right. Guinness...</i>

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.010
<i>That moment... It was that moment.</i>

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.470
We'll get that Guinness record
another time, okay?

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.730
Is something wrong?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.350
I remembered something.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:36.730
Miki has a girlfriend named Mina Hiraya.
Do you know her?

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:42.450
I heard Hiraya transferred to HQ.

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:45.910
I'm a little chilly. Let's go inside.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:52.620
<i>No way.</i>

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:54.670
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.590
<i>Aya is Aya!</i>

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.090
<i>That's impossible.</i>

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:18.320
Okay, Ogata. Can you read the rest?

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:23.320
Oh, sorry. I didn't...

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:28.030
O-Okay, Matoba, can you do it?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:28.990
Okay.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.830
That Suzuki's such a jerk!

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.500
She told Sayaka to read from the textbook,
knowing she can't talk!

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:39.960
That's really awful.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.930
"It's not the teacher's fault.
It's my fault," she says.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:47.050
Is that true?

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.180
It's not your fault, Ogata.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.020
Don't let it bother you.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:53.020
That's right!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.770
But hey, isn't that kind of like bullying?
That's a problem!

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:01.440
"It's not like that!
The teacher didn't mean anything by it.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:04.150
Let's stop talking about it," she says.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.070
Is that true?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.870
But-- Oh, I'm sorry!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.280
Are you okay?

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.950
Sorry, Sayaka. Let's go wash that off.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.960
Oh, I'll go too.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.370
You stay here.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:20.290
It's so amazing how you can tell
what Sayaka wants to say.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.710
Is it the power of love?

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.170
N-No, it's not. I can just kind of tell.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.390
But what's gotten into Sayaka?

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:33.100
She was absent for three months,
and now that she's back, she can't talk?

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:38.100
I heard something bad happened
to a relative, but no details.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.940
I think she's getting a little better now,
right? She's starting to smile more.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.280
That's wrong.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.490
She's not getting better at all.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.240
She's just forcing herself to smile.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.740
I can tell.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.410
She's been fighting.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.750
With deep sadness.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:03.250
Marriage?

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.300
Yes. That's what Marcus wants.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.550
He's not quitting the Shoshidai, is he?

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.510
No, that's not it.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.970
I think he just wants it
to cheer himself up.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.390
I see. This shows you're doing a good job.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.020
You have a good grasp on his heart.

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:22.320
Well done.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.570
Why not?

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.900
It's just some paperwork, right?

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:29.450
And what's more,

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.660
even if he does get married,
he'll be going right back into cold sleep.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.580
It might be for a long while this time.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:40.960
When that happens, I want you
to supervise the next Chrysalis.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.250
The next one?

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.590
Yes. Thanks.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:50.890
I knew it.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:54.390
Mina Hiraya's name isn't listed
at the Shoshidai HQ.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:56.180
Beelzebub.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:58.770
Find her.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.900
A new Chrysalis just arrived.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.410
I want you to supervise him.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.160
-His age is--
-Stop it!

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:15.160
I can't do this. I can't do this anymore!

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.910
How long... how long do I have to do this?

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.710
First Mina Hiraya, then Aya Takagi.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.290
Who am I supposed to be next?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.460
I get another operation, and this time...

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.680
this time, what will my face look like?

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.010
What's wrong?

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:37.640
Thanks to you, both Naoki Miki
and Marcus Lithos were able to be happy.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.560
Even if that love was false.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:43.230
You did a noble job.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.820
It's because of you
that Miki didn't have to die alone.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:51.610
Miki's dead?

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.080
What is this?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.910
Miki didn't die.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.250
The Shoshidai killed him!

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:07.500
Miki.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:10.670
Aya?

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:12.840
I trusted you!

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:14.720
Why?

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.870
Will you come to art club today?

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.830
Hey there, you two.
Having fun being all lovey-dovey today?

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:47.880
Matoba, aren't you being too clingy
with Sayaka just because she can't talk?

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.090
What's your problem?

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:55.340
This is boring.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.240
Marcus! Wh-What's wrong?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.490
You betrayed me.

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.240
You're a liar.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:23.580
What are you talking about?

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:27.920
That's right! Administrator Kagami said
we can get married.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:29.670
Married?

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:31.880
Who would I be marrying?

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.670
Aya Takagi? Mina Hiraya?

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.970
Or someone else?

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.720
Jeez, cut it out Marcus.
What kind of joke is--

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:44.560
Don't lie to me! I know everything!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.020
Did you and Miki ever get
that Guinness record? Well?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.020
I-I don't know what you're talking about!

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.070
You betrayed Miki.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:54.440
You betrayed me.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.490
And you're going to
keep betraying other men.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:01.120
And you're still going to lie to me?
I won't forgive you!

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.830
N-No! It's not like that.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:06.580
You're right. At first it was just a job.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.040
But now I'm serious.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.000
I really love you.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.210
Really?

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:16.670
Marcus.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:32.980
M-Marc... I'm sorry.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.040
You traitor.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.290
Show me your real face!

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:59.430
It can't be! Marcus...

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.550
Yes. After killing Aya Takagi,
he turned into a Busoma.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.140
He's trying to escape the facility!

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.270
<i>Attention all security personnel.</i>

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.940
<i>Marcus Lithos is now designated
<i>Busoma Azoth.</i></i>

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.690
<i>Initiate pursuit!
<i>Use of live ammunition authorized!</i></i>

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.330
Fall back to block 3!

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:34.500
Everyone betrays me.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.090
Erika.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:37.170
Aya.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.710
The Shoshidai.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:10.580
Ogata?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:25.510
Release Chrysalis numbers Alpha 0301,
0303, and 0402 from cold sleep.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.140
They will pursue the Busoma Azoth!
